   ],
   "allies": [],
   "brief": [
    {
     "chara": 58,
     "text": "The day the machine broke, its last cycle ran far too long. One soul was washed so clean that nothing was left of who it had been. It went out into the world new."
    },
    {
     "chara": 58,
     "text": "I felt you arrive, {name}. I didn't know what you were, only that the Malice couldn't find a single handhold on you. I'm sorry I never said."
    },
    {
     "chara": "player",
     "text": "So that thing is everything they scrubbed out of people. And I'm what's left when the scrubbing works."
    },
    {
     "chara": 59,
     "text": "Janemba is every yesterday that was ever thrown away. You are the only one with no yesterday at all. It cannot open you."
    },
    {
     "chara": 58,
     "text": "We'll lure it into the Hyperbolic Time Chamber and shut the door: a world with no outside. Only you can go in. I'll be right here when you come out."
    }
   ],
   "intro": [
    {
     "speaker": "narrator",
     "text": "The Hyperbolic Time Chamber. Endless white. Then a stain spreads across it: red sky, black trees, Hell painting itself over nothing."
